      "description": {
        "simpleText": "In this installment of AMR’s Three Questions series, Chris Gordon sits down with Kathy Clow, whose work quietly spans continents, callings, and seasons of life. Kathy and her husband John have served with Mission to the World for nearly twenty-five years, most recently in Central America, where Kathy has long been involved in missionary care and encouragement.\n\nIn the conversation, Kathy reflects on life and ministry shaped by long obedience, the formation that comes through counseling work, and what it means to care well for marriages, families, and women serving faithfully across the global church."
